Privacy Policy for SYNC: Logic Path Puzzle
Last updated: October 30, 2026
The current policy for Path Puzzle (previously SYNC / Zip) is at https://tlldevelopers.github.io/PRIVACY_POLICIES/path-puzzle/ (English and Spanish).

1. Introduction
We at TLL Developers ("we," "our," or "us") are committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and safeguard your information when you use our mobile application SYNC: Logic Path Puzzle (the "App").

By using the App, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy. If you do not agree with the terms of this privacy policy, please do not access the application.

2. Information We Collect
a. Personal Data We do not knowingly collect personally identifiable information (PII) such as your name, address, or phone number. We do not require you to create an account to play the game.

b. Non-Personal Data & Game Progress To improve your gaming experience, we may collect non-personal data such as:

Game Progress: Levels completed, stars earned, and high scores. This data is stored locally on your device or via cloud save services if enabled.

Device Information: Device model, operating system version, and unique device identifiers (Advertising ID).

c. Third-Party Services We may use third-party services that collect information used to identify you. The links to the privacy policies of the third-party service providers used by the App are listed below:

Google Play Services (for authentication, achievements, and cloud saves)

AdMob / Unity Ads (if the app displays ads in the future)

Firebase Analytics (for crash reporting and usage analysis)

3. How We Use Your Information
We use the collected data for the following purposes:

To provide and maintain the App's functionality.

To save your progress (Campaign Mode) and game settings.

To detect, prevent, and address technical issues (bugs and crashes).

To improve the game design based on anonymous usage trends.

4. Cookies and Tracking Technologies
The App does not use "cookies" explicitly. However, the App may use third-party code and libraries (like Google AdMob or Analytics) that use "cookies" or similar tracking technologies to collect information and improve their services. You have the option to either accept or refuse these identifiers within your device settings.

5. Children’s Privacy
Our App is designed for general audiences. We do not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from children under 13. In the case we discover that a child under 13 has provided us with personal information, we immediately delete this from our servers. If you are a parent or guardian and you are aware that your child has provided us with personal information, please contact us so that we will be able to do necessary actions.

6. Security
We value your trust in providing us your Personal Information, thus we are striving to use commercially acceptable means of protecting it. But remember that no method of transmission over the internet, or method of electronic storage is 100% secure and reliable, and we cannot guarantee its absolute security.

7. GDPR & CCPA Compliance
GDPR (Users in the European Union): You have the right to access, rectify, or erase your personal data. Since we do not store personal data on our own servers, you can manage your data primarily through your device settings or Google account settings.

CCPA (Users in California): You have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information. Our App respects "Do Not Sell" requests configured via your device settings regarding advertising IDs.

Data processed by third-party SDKs (as declared in Google Play Data safety)

This section lists, for SYNC / Path Puzzle, the data processed by the third-party SDKs included in the app. It matches the Data safety form of the app on Google Play.

- Google AdMob (advertising): collects and shares with Google the advertising ID / app set ID and other device identifiers, an approximate location derived from your IP address, ad interactions (impressions, clicks) and diagnostics (such as app launches and performance). Purposes: advertising, ad measurement and analytics, and fraud prevention and security. We do not receive your name or contact details from AdMob.
- Firebase Analytics (Google): app interactions (events and screens viewed), the Firebase installation ID / device identifiers, and basic device and app information. Purposes: analytics and app functionality.
- Firebase Crashlytics (Google): crash logs and diagnostics (stack trace, device model, Android and app version, a random installation ID). Purposes: analytics and app stability.
- Firebase Cloud Messaging (Google): a push token / Firebase installation ID, used to deliver notifications. Purpose: app functionality.

Consent: where required (European Economic Area, United Kingdom, Switzerland) the app asks for your consent through Google's User Messaging Platform (UMP) before showing ads.
Ad choices: you can reset or delete your advertising ID and opt out of ads personalisation in Android Settings > Google > Ads.
Security: data sent to these services travels encrypted in transit (HTTPS/TLS).
Data deletion: the app has no user accounts. Data stored on your device is deleted by uninstalling the app or clearing its data; for data held by Google (advertising ID, analytics), reset your advertising ID as described above or write to tll.developers.apps@gmail.com and we will help with the request.

